<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="How the Cortxt public website handles cookies, local preferences, hosting metadata, and external services." />
    <title>Privacy & trust | Cortxt</title>
    <script src="/landing-theme.js" is:inline></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="nav shell">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Cortxt home"><span>C</span>Cortxt</a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/docs/">Docs</a><a class="nav-cta" href="https://github.com/rian010194/cortxt">GitHub</a></nav>
    </header>
    <main class="policy-page shell">
      <p class="eyebrow"><i></i> Privacy &amp; trust</p>
      <h1>Clear boundaries.<br /><em>No tracking theatre.</em></h1>
      <p class="policy-intro">This statement describes the public website at cortxt.io as it operates today. It is a factual product statement, not a compliance certification or legal opinion.</p>

      <section class="policy-summary">
        <article><span>Tracking cookies</span><strong>None set by Cortxt</strong><p>No advertising, cross-site tracking, visitor analytics, or marketing pixels are included.</p></article>
        <article><span>Browser storage</span><strong>Theme preference only</strong><p>The landing-page theme selector stores its preset id in local storage on your device. It is not sent to Cortxt.</p></article>
        <article><span>Accounts &amp; forms</span><strong>None on this site</strong><p>The public site has no Cortxt account, newsletter, contact form, or hosted customer workspace.</p></article>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-copy">
        <h2>What infrastructure may process</h2>
        <p>The site is delivered through Cloudflare Pages. Like ordinary web hosting, the provider receives request metadata such as IP address, user agent, requested URL, timestamps, and security signals needed to deliver and protect the service. Cloudflare may apply strictly necessary security mechanisms under its own terms. Cortxt does not use that data for advertising or visitor profiling.</p>

        <h2>External destinations</h2>
        <p>Links to GitHub, Cloudflare-hosted previews, and other external services leave the Cortxt site. Those services operate under their own privacy and cookie policies. Do not include private or customer data in a public GitHub issue.</p>

        <h2>The software and your data</h2>
        <p>The open-source Cortxt software is separate from this public website. Local or self-hosted deployments process the repositories, providers, credentials, workspaces, and evidence that their operator configures. Operators are responsible for the privacy, retention, access, and lawful-processing rules of those deployments.</p>

        <h2>If this changes</h2>
        <p>Before Cortxt adds hosted accounts, analytics, contact forms, or non-essential cookies, this statement must be updated with the controller identity, purposes, legal bases, recipients, retention periods, rights-request route, and any consent controls required for that processing.</p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>For project-level questions, use the <a href="https://github.com/rian010194/cortxt">Cortxt repository</a>. Do not post personal data in public issues. A private privacy-rights contact will be published before Cortxt operates a hosted account or customer-data service.</p>

        <h2>Reference principles</h2>
        <p>This statement follows the EU transparency principle that people should receive concise, intelligible information about what data is processed and why. See the European Commission&rsquo;s guidance on <a href="https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection/information-business-and-organisations/obligations_en">transparency obligations</a> and <a href="https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection/information-business-and-organisations/principles-gdpr_en">data protection by design and by default</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: 27 August 2026</p>
    </main>
    <footer class="shell"><a class="brand" href="/"><span>C</span>Cortxt</a><span>Privacy by restraint.</span><a href="/">Home -&gt;</a></footer>
  </body>
</html>
